WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.373
- I was born in Windsor Castle.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.230
Queen Victoria herself
was present at my birth.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.430
- [Interviewer] Was she?

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.250
- Everyone thought I was a slow child.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.360
- [Interviewer] Slow?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.780
In which sense? Walking?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.613
- No, dear.

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:20.840
(coughing)

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.143
Slow in here.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:25.263
- Right.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.123
- I was born deaf.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.593
- Oh, I'm sorry.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.821
But otherwise perfectly normal.

00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:36.417
- Well, I thought so.

00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:38.270
But obviously, others didn't because

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.660
then I was diagnosed with schizophrenia

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.103
and sent to an asylum.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.930
- A mental asylum?

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:50.763
- Yes.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.273
I was treated by Sigmund Freud.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.683
He was not a kind man.

00:01:09.022 --> 00:01:12.022
(suspenseful music)

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:13.713
- Go on.

00:01:16.482 --> 00:01:18.732
- [Alice] I was there
for just over two years

00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:22.537
and I managed to escape

00:01:22.537 --> 00:01:25.204
(clock ticking)

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:31.350
and went back to Athens.
(typewriter clicking)

00:01:42.919 --> 00:01:43.752
(phone ringing)

00:01:43.752 --> 00:01:46.752
(suspenseful music)

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.785
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:55.614 --> 00:02:58.281
(clock ticking)

00:03:06.265 --> 00:03:07.515
- [Alice] Amen.

00:03:24.832 --> 00:03:25.832
- Bubbikins.

00:03:37.004 --> 00:03:40.421
(Philip clearing throat)

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:48.630
- It is a common staple
of mother-in-law jokes

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.130
that having one come
to stay is a nightmare,

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.860
but having this mother-in-law to stay

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.010
can only be a blessing.

00:03:56.979 --> 00:03:58.290
- Oh.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.260
- For Princess Alice is
that rarest of creatures,

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.500
a member of a royal
family that has suffered

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.650
more than the rest of us, worked
harder than the rest of us,

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.763
and created more good than the rest of us.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.990
Congenitally deaf, she was
consistently misunderstood,

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:22.163
marginalized, and underestimated.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.597
Doctors inflicted untold horrors on her,

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:29.244
x-raying her womb to bring on menopause

00:04:29.244 --> 00:04:30.870
and reduce her libido

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:42.060
and electroshock treatment
to treat her hysteria,

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.750
but instead of business,
Princess Alice dedicated

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.059
her life to charity work, public service,

00:04:48.059 --> 00:04:50.630
and campaigning for social justice,

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.873
often at great personal risk.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.783
Well, it goes on and on, it's,

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.523
it's a love letter.

